   </text:sequence-decls>
   <text:p text:style-name="P1">User Data Management in Scriptoria</text:p>
   <text:h text:style-name="P2" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark text:name="_xxgyl1snssx1" />Introduction</text:h>
   <text:p text:style-name="P3">In April 2023, Google Play announced the new <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/10144311" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">account deletion requirements</text:a> and added new Data deletion questions within your Data safe<text:span text:style-name="T1">t</text:span>y form. <text:span text:style-name="T1">See </text:span><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/13327111/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link"><text:span text:style-name="T1">Understanding Google Play’s app account deletion requirements</text:span></text:a><text:span text:style-name="T1"> for more details.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P4" />
   <text:p text:style-name="P5">In the App Builders, on the <text:span text:style-name="T2">Data &amp; Analytics</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T3"></text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T2">User Accounts</text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T3"></text:span> <text:span text:style-name="T2">Data Deletion</text:span> configuration page, you can specify the Data Deletion URLs that will be included in the data-safety.csv, which can be imported into Google Play to answer the <text:span text:style-name="T4">questions. If you are using Scriptoria, </text:span><text:span text:style-name="T5">leave these fields blank and Scriptoria will provide pages for the end user to submit data deletion requests.</text:span></text:p>
   <text:p text:style-name="P5" />
